Enable SPI_IMX + IMX_SDMA on iMX8MP (base drivers, no firmware bake-in).

CONFIG_SPI_IMX is required for /dev/spidev<bus>.<cs> to materialise when
the Toradex DT overlay verdin-imx8mp_spidev_overlay.dtbo is pre-applied
to the guest DTB at capsule build time. The overlay attaches a spidev@0
child (compatible "rohm,dh2228fv") under ecspi1, but without
CONFIG_SPI_IMX no driver claims the controller and the spidev child
is never bound.

CONFIG_IMX_SDMA is also required because the ecspi1 DT node references
`dmas = <&sdma1 ...>` (rx/tx channels). Without the SDMA driver, sdma1
never probes and ecspi1 stays in deferred-probe forever:

    platform 30820000.spi: deferred probe pending

CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE is NOT touched here. The SDMA firmware bake-in
into vmlinux is only needed by the dev-lvgl capsule on Torizon (where
imx-sdma requests its firmware at ~2.3 s, before the OSTree rootfs
pivot at ~4.7 s — the minimal initramfs does not carry it). Capsules
that ship a full rootfs from t=0 (e.g. bsp-linux / e1c-fc) can load
sdma-imx7d.bin from /usr/lib/firmware/ normally, so the bake-in is
scoped via a defconfig fragment in meta-e1c-dev-lvgl/recipes-linux/
linux/files/e1c-dev-lvgl-verdin.cfg rather than forced into every
verdin kernel.

Signed-off-by: EDGEMTech <info@edgemtech.ch>

--- a/arch/arm64/configs/verdin_imx8mp_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/verdin_imx8mp_defconfig
@@ -2820,7 +2820,7 @@
 # CONFIG_SPI_FSL_QUADSPI is not set
 # CONFIG_SPI_NXP_FLEXSPI is not set
 CONFIG_SPI_GPIO=y
-# CONFIG_SPI_IMX is not set
+CONFIG_SPI_IMX=y
 # CONFIG_SPI_FSL_SPI is not set
 # CONFIG_SPI_MICROCHIP_CORE is not set
 # CONFIG_SPI_MICROCHIP_CORE_QSPI is not set
@@ -5384,7 +5384,7 @@
 # CONFIG_FSL_QDMA is not set
 CONFIG_FSL_EDMA_V3=y
 # CONFIG_IMX_DMA is not set
-# CONFIG_IMX_SDMA is not set
+CONFIG_IMX_SDMA=y
 # CONFIG_INTEL_IDMA64 is not set
 # CONFIG_MV_XOR_V2 is not set
 CONFIG_MXS_DMA=y
